Z||000003||862M4inCA||07-26-2001||08:23 AM||||I think I know the piece your talking about and it's round.....If this is correct try turning your hazard lights on, and see if you can feel the contacts open and close, if not, also try the turn signal. Something wants to tell me they used a separate flasher for each system.||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||07-26-2001||08:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 862M4inCA:<BR><B>Something wants to tell me they used a separate flasher for each system.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>FWIW, one of those "somethings" is the factory wiring diagram.  In other words, you're correct - the hazard flasher is not the same one used to flash the directional signals.<BR>||||reg||14
